            "width": 1280
          }
        ],
        "name": "Herbert Ong",
        "text": "SpaceX just guided to a $35B quarter! The CFO sees $33B to $37B in Q1 2027 revenue, up from $14.6B this quarter. That's more than double in just two quarters.\n\n• SI revenue was $7.56B, up 830%, and it's now bigger than Starlink\n\n• 13 GW of compute expected by the end of 2027\n\n• Grok Bot has 800K paid weekly users, more than doubling in a month\n\n• Starship Flight 15 will try to catch both stages in mid-November\n\n• Starlink is in talks for 80,000+ US cell sites\n\nSo why did $SPCX stock drop?  👇",
