      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "Naval Ravikant once shared a story about Bill Gates shorting Tesla, a bet that could ultimately cost him more than $10 billion.\n\nGates had taken a massive short position against Tesla, reportedly equivalent to roughly 1% of the company’s total shares.\n\nNaval suggested that if Tesla became the world’s most valuable company by a wide margin, the losses could be so enormous that even someone as wealthy as Bill Gates could face financial ruin.\n\nBut what fascinated Naval wasn't the money. It was Elon Musk’s reaction.\n\nMusk was genuinely confused. How could someone who publicly championed clean energy financially bet against a company working to accelerate the world's transition to sustainable energy?\n\nTo Gates, it was reportedly just a financial decision. But to Musk, it was something much deeper.\n\nAccording to Naval, that moment revealed something fundamental about Elon Musk.\n\nElon Musk is not driven by money, wealth, or status. He is driven by a mission.\n\nThe billions he earns are not trophies. They are tools.\n\nTools to build rockets, revolutionize transportation, advance technology, and ultimately make humanity a multiplanetary civilization.\nhttps://x.com/iam_smx/status/2005348612344005081/video/1",
